      "description": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Governance Lab at New York University&rsquo;s Tandon School of Engineering, &ldquo;GovLab&rdquo;, is an action research center whose mission is to strengthen the ability of institutions &ndash; including but not limited to governments &ndash; and people to work more openly, collaboratively, effectively and legitimately to make better decisions and solve public problems. The GovLab has examined a range of issues on the use and application of AI technologies, from identifying citizens&rsquo; needs by </span><a href=\"https://blog.thegovlab.org/post/new-report-identifying-citizens-needs-by-combining-artificial-intelligence-ai-and-collective-intelligence-ci\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">combining artificial intelligence (AI) and collective intelligence (CI)</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to our latest project on </span><a href=\"https://ailocalism.org/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">AI Localism</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, which refers to the actions taken by local decision-makers to address the use of AI within a city or community.</span></p>",
      "url": "https://www.thegovlab.org/"
    },
